":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM MST this afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood http://cotrip.org","ends":"2026-11-04T05:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.089a310d5f6b73825563e3a8cfaf9f90b6b00b53.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.089a310d5f6b73825563e3a8cfaf9f90b6b00b53.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T18:24:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 011824 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1124 AM MST Sun Nov 1 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Significant and dangerous flooding is expected to start today across portions of the San Juan Mountains and adjacent San Luis Valley. - Heavy and wet snow is expected across the San Juan Mountains late tonight into tomorrow morning. - Unsettled pattern continues t","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T07:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 010707 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueb